WEBVTT

NOTE
Synthetic platform-neutral daily standup transcript
Sprint 01 | Day 02 of 10 | 2026-04-07 | Focus: Catalog search filters

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:57.000
<v Jane Doe>Morning, folks. Day 02 of the sprint. We’ve got a build in test, but we lost half a day on the result count. Sarah, can you get to the dashboard now?

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:59.000
<v Sarah Miller>Yes, finally. Release-viewer came through late yesterday. I can see the reports but not download the trace, so I’ve requested one more permission.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:03:01.000
<v Robert Taylor>That’s a third role for the same environment. The access note just said “catalog access.” I’ll write down the exact group names; I assumed they were bundled.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:04:03.000
<v David Wilson>The filter UI is integrated. I saw count 24, then 18, then 24 again when I moved the price slider quickly. It’s an old response overwriting the new one.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:57.000
<v Michael Brown>The API responses are right. They’re just coming back out of order.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:06:07.000
<v David Wilson>Yep, that’s frontend. I’ll compare the request key before applying a response. I thought cancelling fetch would be enough, but it isn’t.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:07:09.000
<v Sarah Miller>I can reproduce it every time with a quick slider drag. I’ll keep the case; it’s a real customer-facing one.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:08:11.000
<v Alex Smith>Good catch. Also, the contract page still says count is after pagination in one paragraph. I updated the table but missed the example.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:09:13.000
<v Michael Brown>I copied that example into my PR. I’ll fix it. Sorry, I should’ve followed the table.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:10:15.000
<v John Doe>Product is asking for a “sort by relevance” option now. It isn’t in this sprint goal. Can we leave it out?

00:10:13.000 --> 00:11:09.000
<v David Wilson>Please. I already have the empty state and accessibility pass queued. Sorting touches the same control and tests.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:12:19.000
<v John Doe>Agreed, I’ll put it in the follow-up list after this release. I should’ve raised it before it got into the ticket comments.

00:12:32.000 --> 00:13:21.000
<v Emily Davis>The larger catalog dataset shows a broad price range is slower, but within the current target. I haven’t checked it with availability on; the shared environment was being redeployed.

00:13:34.000 --> 00:14:23.000
<v Robert Taylor>The redeploy was for a certificate update. The service came back, but the dashboard permissions didn’t. I’m adding a post-reset permission check.

00:14:36.000 --> 00:15:25.000
<v Sarah Miller>That would’ve saved me a lot of time yesterday.

00:15:38.000 --> 00:16:27.000
<v Alex Smith>The API PR has two reviews waiting. I can take the contract part now, but I still owe the payment review. Could Emily approve the query plan and I do the behavior?

00:16:25.000 --> 00:17:21.000
<v Emily Davis>Yes. I’ve got the query result. I can approve the query change, but Sarah should verify the response values.

00:17:42.000 --> 00:18:31.000
<v Sarah Miller>I’ll rerun count, null stock, and the race case once David’s patch lands.

00:18:44.000 --> 00:19:33.000
<v Jane Doe>We did the short contract walkthrough this sprint and it helped, but we didn’t check the dashboard role or the old example. I’ll add both to the ready-to-test checklist.

00:19:46.000 --> 00:20:35.000
<v David Wilson>I’ll have the request-key fix up before lunch. If the API changes again, please tag me on the page update, not just the ticket.
